==== via EVA bootloader ====


To install OpenWrt via Eva bootloader, within the first seconds after power on an ftp connection needs to be established to the FRITZ!Box at   192.168.178.1 and the the following ftp commands need to be run:

<code>
  ftp> quote USER adam2
  ftp> quote PASS adam2
  ftp> binary
  ftp> debug
  ftp> passive
  ftp> quote MEDIA FLSH
  ftp> put /path/to/openwrt-lantiq-xway-avm_fritz7312-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin mtd1
  ftp> quote REBOOT
</code>


Please mind that this instruction requests the **sysupgrade** image to be flashed to mtd1, not the initramfs image!


==== via fritzflash ====

See [[docs/guide-user/installation/installation_methods/fritzflash]]

from the linked page [[https://fritz-tools.readthedocs.io/en/latest/flashing/general.html#selecting-the-right-image]]:

> Selecting the right Image
> Gluon builds by default factory and sysupgrade images. AVM devices don’t need special factory-images, so most of them are flashed via the sysupgrade images.

-> use the **sysupgrade** image



===== Hardware =====
==== Info ====
^ [[wp>Instruction set|Architecture]]  | [[wp>MIPS architecture|MIPS]] |
^ Vendor                               | [[wp>Lantiq]]  |
^ [[docs:techref:bootloader]]          | [[docs:techref:bootloader:adam2|Adam2]] |
^ [[docs:techref:hardware:soc|System-On-Chip]]   | Lantiq Xway ARX188 PSB 50812 EL (MIPS 34Kc) |
^ [[docs:techref:hardware:cpu|CPU]]/Speed        | 2x393 MHz |
^ NOR Flash       | [[https://media.digikey.com/pdf/Data%20Sheets/Macronix/MX29GL128E.pdf|Macronix MX29GL128EHT2I-90G]], 16MiB |
^ RAM Chip        | [[http://61.222.70.43/upload/product/datasheet_11_2013-02-22_11-03-36.2_Zentel|Zentel A4S12D40FTP-G5]] |
^ RAM Specs       | DDR1 64MiB @ 196 MHz       |
^ Wireless        | Atheros AR9227 b/g/n 2x2   |
^ Ethernet        | 1x 10/100 Atheros AR8030-A |
^ Switch          | none (only 1 ethernet port available) |
^ xDSL            | lantiq ADSL2+ |
^ USB             | no            |
^ DECT            | [[http://www.dialog-semiconductor.com/sites/default/files/datasheet_sc14441_0.pdf|dialog semiconductor SC14441]] |
^ Serial          | Yes (2.54mm, unpopulated) |
^ GPIO Buttons    | wifi rfkill, dect rfkill  |
^ Power           | External 5V 1.6A          |

===== Opening the case =====

Towards the back of the device there are two (one on each side) plastic latches.\\
Those are accessible through the ventilation slots:\\
{{https://abload.de/img/2015-10-0413.21.264lup5.jpg?400|}}

Use a thin tool (screw driver or similar) to push them towards the inside of the device.\\
Once you push it far enough you can open the case a little on one side, then do the same on the other side -> the two parts of the case will "fall apart" on their own.

